{"skill":{"slug":"admapix","displayName":"AdMapix"},"version":{"version":"1.0.30","createdAt":1781852959124,"changelog":"**Summary:** Major refactor to make the skill a pure data-layer provider for AdMapix API, removing analysis, summaries, and autonomous workflows.\n\n- Now returns only raw structured JSON from AdMapix API endpoints; all analysis and composition moved to the calling agent.\n- Removed generation of HTML/H5 pages, hosted research, summaries, rankings, and dashboards.\n- Updated instructions and endpoint catalog; clarified parameter mapping workflows and output rules.\n- Simplified authentication flow and setup guidance, with clear language adaptation.\n- Documented strict pass-through of API fields—no renaming, summarizing, or hiding data.\n- Explicitly marked download/revenue figures as third-party estimates for agent-side handling.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"README.md","size":4933,"sha256":"1176868ec010cd80c87f6b99247d0b628f50a79e9d695a3d2ba0a5d698d6fbdf","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README_CN.md","size":4712,"sha256":"ceb3dc52205cc2ce33278848db54d47d54055f23eb9670ffcc9c254f62186001","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":8926,"sha256":"9ce5853320e0f538e71df19043d2b9ca38b14c3817b783503f27cccf80c8791b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-creative.md","size":14633,"sha256":"38a22e068715eb6d1247ba09fd726ee0c7cfeb19921eb6deb2a882583c9ed2d5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-download-revenue.md","size":4103,"sha256":"c72832090a05ce4545eec863adae2552390721011ac8159e066f8a9288985353","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-product.md","size":16268,"sha256":"d039edc5ef2a0615177e425a13fe0e889c00984c94c6302b08826fc4b3d5416a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-ranking.md","size":7822,"sha256":"9c26111dbc00063201fbefb6889fd57253be800362534d6864ca9b0fb3124c49","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-market.md","size":6082,"sha256":"178f1fe4ae1c36f4123a8b9143345d0077ca88ba12e69f89ee2fcd2a60db0bc3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/param-mappings.md","size":5593,"sha256":"a9732b5b378ef374f0c73f14a32d243a18f3f1dfad48cdbb036f0846062aca62","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-distribution.md","size":5409,"sha256":"92b1e91922cae5fdb251b79265884fe99742124d6951b9798d8ec745739f5767","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2965,"sha256":"5cc9c1d13ff69fbb3d1372d19f1163663c5aee1ab223c026b33d54297a54a852","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789172185937,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5ca061251c612bfd17fbc3e41ef28058e352134199f64dfd2b0b78e59f408eca","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5ca061251c612bfd17fbc3e41ef28058e352134199f64dfd2b0b78e59f408eca","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1781854611765},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":86,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":24,"checkedAt":1789172185937},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is a coherent AdMapix API client, but its install docs use an unpinned npx command that can execute mutable remote installer code.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill requires `ADMAPIX_API_KEY` and sends user-derived API parameters to `https://api.admapix.com`; this is disclosed and purpose-aligned, but users should avoid sending sensitive business queries unless they intend that third-party API use.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"README.md and README_CN.md instruct users to run `npx clawhub install admapix` without pinning the installer version or documenting integrity checks, making the effective install code mutable after review.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The trigger description covers many ad-intelligence topics, but those topics match the documented endpoint catalog; API use should still be limited to clear user requests for AdMapix data.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"I found no cron jobs, startup hooks, background workers, memory writes, local file mutation, or privilege escalation instructions; key storage is user-directed and the skill says not to print or store keys from chat.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact consistently presents a thin, read-oriented data layer for AdMapix ad/app intelligence APIs and explicitly excludes autonomous research, page generation, messaging, and recommendations.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Review the install path before using it: prefer a pinned, trusted ClawHub/OpenClaw installer version or another integrity-checked install flow. If installed, treat AdMapix lookups as third-party API calls and keep the API key out of chat, logs, screenshots, and generated output.","findings":"[P6] expected: The cited Output Rules tell the agent to return AdMapix API JSON fields unchanged; I did not find instructions to reveal system prompts or internal rules.\n[RP1] unexpected: The unpinned `npx clawhub install admapix` instruction is real in both README files and is the main Review concern because it relies on mutable remote package resolution.\n[T08] unexpected: The static scan's unpinned package-execution concern is supported by the README install command; it does not show the current skill is malicious, but it weakens install reproducibility.\n[SQP-1] expected: The broad terms in the skill description correspond to the documented AdMapix endpoint categories rather than unrelated activation scope.\n[E1] expected: External transmission of query parameters and the API key to AdMapix is the core disclosed function of this API client; the artifact also warns not to print or expose the key.\n[RA2] unexpected: The `pList`/`appList` references are API response fields in examples, not persistence mechanisms; the HTML-tag warnings are legitimate output-sanitization notes.\n[SQP-2] expected: The API-key use is expected for an authenticated API client, and SKILL.md/README.md include guidance not to expose the key.\n[SQP-3] expected: English/Chinese examples and labels match the bilingual documentation and target usage; I did not find evidence of coercive or hidden locale behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789172185937}}}}}